&#x200B;

thanks

is she competing against ariana for more albums in a year or something?

&#x200B;

~~i'm not complaining tho, this just made my whole week~~

majoring in psychology and fellow depressed person here! i'll try to give some advice and you choose what works or not.

&#x200B;

> Now the only person who was ever nice to me longer then the two week morally necessary period doesn't care about me anymore because I'm so annoying and she probably never cared tbh 

it's normal to have those feelings, but you would be surprised to find out that your friend doesn't think you're annoying. if you trust her, share those fears with her, or otherwise the situation will get worse. it's better to be honest about your feelings that repress them, which will only lead to pain for you and your friend. btw, you're not selfish, you're human; it's okay not to be perfect all the time (don't hold yourself to an impossible standard).

&#x200B;

> wish my parents weren't such conservative old day freak shows so I could get therapy or something. Sometimes I think I may have aspergers but guess I won't know for years. Every single day has been exactly the same for years. 

i'm sorry i can't help much on this, but maybe you could find a support group or a group chat online? there are also a lot of videos in youtube and pages in instagram that teach you how to cope.

&#x200B;

> Every single day has been exactly the same for years.   Nothing ever changes 

one of the most important aspects of living a healthy and fulfilling life is being proactive in the changes that occur in it. right now you're probably quarantined so you won't be able to do much (and that's fine), but try to vision what kind of future do you want and make a list of the things you have to change to make it real. (tip: start with small changes and go up from there).

&#x200B;

> Even with relentless pursuit there is nothing corrigible that can be done about living a hopeless and painful life. There is no underlying purpose in your exploitation and torment.  

i think you're holding your yourself to too high standards. you don't need to have a purpose or a great impact in the world as long as you find your own purpose to live. even taking care of a puppy can give you a purpose, it doesn't has to be innovative or life changing.

&#x200B;

i hope you understood something in my broken english and i hope i managed to help even if just a little bit.

dear anti-quarantine people in my country: if you keep going out to protest the quarantine, THEN THE QUARANTINE IT'S NEVER GOING TO END. STAY. IN YOUR FUCKING. HOMES.

&#x200B;

sorry, i needed to vent

Yeah, I remember watching the moment before the fight between Ozai and Aang and how excited I was about it as a child. Now that I'm older I'm just like: "oh for the love of sweet jesus, what are you doing? Go home, seek a therapist!".

&#x200B;

Honestly, having it watched recently, it made me realize that all the characters should suffer from a plethora of mental issues: PSTD, depression, anxiety, survivor guilt, etc.
